  "goodToKnow": "Die Seenot is distress at sea: in Seenot geraten. Germany's Seenotretter, the DGzRS founded in 1865, operate rescue cruisers on the North Sea and Baltic, funded entirely by donations, including from small boat-shaped collection boxes. Private Seenotrettung of migrants in the Mediterranean is a politically contested topic. Die See (feminine) means sea, der See (masculine) lake. It has no plural."
